<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><title>{title}</title><meta name="description" content="Learn what makes American Mah Jongg unique, from tiles and jokers to the Charleston and yearly pattern cards."/><link rel="canonical" href="https://mymahjongera.com/learn/american-mahjong/"/><style>body{font:18px/1.75 Arial,sans-serif;margin:0;background:#fffaf7;color:#4d2540}main{max-width:770px;margin:60px auto;padding:0 24px}h1{font: bold clamp(38px,6vw,60px)/1.1 Georgia,serif}h2{font-family:Georgia,serif;margin-top:44px}a{color:#ad4270}nav{padding:22px;background:#fce8ee}</style></head><body><nav><a href="/">← My Mahjong Era</a></nav><main><p>LEARN · AMERICAN MAHJONG</p><h1>American Mahjong: a friendly beginner's guide</h1><p>New to American Mah Jongg? You're in the right place. It is usually played by four people and combines familiar Mahjong tiles with special features such as jokers and a yearly hand card.</p><h2>What do you need?</h2><p>A set suited to American Mah Jongg, four racks, a table and a current official hand card for each player. Players usually use 152 tiles including eight jokers, although sets and house rules may vary.</p><h2>What is the goal?</h2><p>Players build a legal combination listed on the current annual card. Unlike many other Mahjong variants, American play depends on these published hand patterns, so a traditional Chinese or Japanese winning hand might not qualify.</p><h2>What is the Charleston?</h2><p>The Charleston is an opening tile-passing sequence often used before play begins. Learn the passing directions and optional steps with your group before starting.</p><h2>What about jokers?</h2><p>Jokers can substitute in eligible groups of matching tiles, subject to the card and league rules. They are not universal wildcards for every tile grouping.</p><h2>Start with people, not perfection</h2><p>For your first game, gather three patient friends, agree which rules and yearly card you're using, and learn one small section of the card together. A teacher or experienced player can make the first evening far more enjoyable.</p><p><strong>Important:</strong> This independently written introduction is not an official NMJL rules publication and does not reproduce the official annual card. Consult current official materials for authoritative hands and exceptions.</p><p><a href="/">Return home</a> · <a href="/lifestyle/mahjong-night/">Plan a Mahjong night</a></p></main></body></html>